Z||000000||BAM-BAM||04-27-2000||10:24 PM||||   I  have been investigating the Extrude Hone process of porting and polishing. I was wondering if anyone knows what kind of HP gains are associated with this process. Is it worth the expense to do this on a 2.8L that is stroked and bored? What knid of Hp numbers could be expected? Would it be comparable to a 3.4L swap? I need some expert advise. You guys are the best source I know. TIA for any replys.<P> Thanx, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||04-28-2000||08:32 AM||||my intake manifolds (upper, lower) have been Extrudehoned. It's was $361 (including shipping) and there was VERY little measureable HP or Torque increase.. off the bottle... ON the bottle there was about a 7lbft increase just because of the increased volume I'm sure if the car was S/C or turbo it would have made a MUCH bigger difference. I'd just take the stock unit off port match it with a set of Fel-Pro gaskets get a new ported Throttle body and be ok with that. and save yourself the money... I wasn't to impressed. I'm sure it would work WONDERS on a bigger displacment motor.. 5 liter. (302) - 5.7 liter (350).. etc but our tiny 2.8 (173), just isn't pulling enought air. Save you money...<P>oh yeah... there is a 6 week turn around!<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 04-28-2000).]||||reg||1
